---
const team = [
  {
    name: 'Aariz Ahmed',
    role: 'Lead Photographer',
    city: 'Lahore',
    src: '/images/about.webp',
    alt: 'Couple in traditional attire smiling together against a plain wall',
    w: 900,
    h: 1350,
  },
  {
    name: 'Sana Malik',
    role: 'Films & Drone',
    city: 'Karachi',
    src: '/images/gallery-12.webp',
    alt: 'Bride and groom in traditional attire posing indoors in modern bridal fashion',
    w: 900,
    h: 1200,
  },
  {
    name: 'Daniyal Raza',
    role: 'Second Shooter',
    city: 'Islamabad',
    src: '/images/gallery-13.webp',
    alt: 'Bride and groom in traditional attire standing together in front of a floral wedding stage',
    w: 900,
    h: 1200,
  },
];
---

<section id="about" class="scroll-mt-24 py-[90px] lg:scroll-mt-[92px]" aria-label="Meet the team">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <p class="reveal text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest2 text-rose">Meet the team</p>
    <h2 class="reveal mt-4 max-w-2xl font-display text-5xl font-normal leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl">
      The people behind the lens
    </h2>

    <div class="reveal mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[1.125rem] leading-relaxed text-body">
      <p>
        Eight years ago I photographed my cousin’s mehndi with a borrowed camera and
        missed half the dances because I was crying behind the lens. I’ve been chasing
        that feeling ever since — across 250+ shaadis, from Lahore marquees to Hunza valleys.
      </p>
      <p>
        My style sits between documentary and editorial: honest, unposed moments, composed
        like the magazine spreads you grew up loving. Warm skin tones, real laughter, and
        not a single awkward “stand there and smile” unless you ask for it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div id="about-more" class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[1.125rem] leading-relaxed text-body" hidden>
      <p class="pt-4">
        Every wedding gets backup cameras, lenses and cards — always. A second shooter joins
        for large multi-day celebrations, and every frame is edited in-house by me, never
        outsourced, so the gallery you receive looks like one person’s careful work. Because
        it is.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sana and Daniyal have shot beside me for five years. Between us we cover the
        bride’s room and the baraat’s entrance, the drone shot at dusk and the grandmother
        asleep in the corner — the whole day, from every angle that matters.
      </p>
    </div>

    <button type="button" id="about-more-btn" class="btn-secondary reveal mt-8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-more">
      Read More About Us
    </button>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-5">
      {team.map((t) => (
        <figure class="reveal">
          <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-[24px]">
            <img
              src={t.src}
              alt={t.alt}
              width={t.w}
              height={t.h}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="aspect-[3/4] w-full object-cover object-top"
            />
            <span class="absolute left-4 top-4 rounded-full bg-rose px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-card">
              {t.role}
            </span>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="mt-4 px-1">
            <span class="block font-bold leading-tight text-ink">{t.name}</span>
            <span class="mt-0.5 block text-sm text-body">{t.city}</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
